WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:02.669
-Thank you, thank you,
thank you. Wow.

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:04.804
I'm excited.
I am very excited to be here.

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:07.439
Been traveling a lot lately.
The year's been going great.

00:00:07.439 --> 00:00:10.310
Seeing these small towns now,
though, type of places

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:11.578
where if you get hungry
after dark,

00:00:11.578 --> 00:00:13.413
you better know how to hunt.

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:14.847
[ Laughter ]

00:00:14.847 --> 00:00:17.250
There's been a lot of learning
experiences, you know?

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.085
You ever heard the saying,
"If you can make it in New York,

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:21.387
you can make it anywhere"?
[ Audience cheering ]

00:00:21.387 --> 00:00:24.557
That's a lie. It's not true.

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:25.858
The second I left the city,

00:00:25.858 --> 00:00:29.128
I seen like five places
I knew I couldn't make it.

00:00:29.128 --> 00:00:31.797
I was just standing on
the highway like, "Not that one.

00:00:31.797 --> 00:00:34.634
Not that one.
I'm definitely gon' die there."

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:35.668
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:36.735
It's been a lot.

00:00:36.735 --> 00:00:38.137
You should make it in New York.

00:00:38.137 --> 00:00:39.839
City's made for you to do so.

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:41.740
Got dollar pizza.

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:44.076
The streets are numbered,

00:00:44.076 --> 00:00:46.078
in order.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.078 --> 00:00:48.981
You got $4 and a [bleep] --
and a high school education,

00:00:48.981 --> 00:00:50.750
you good.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:52.718
You made it.

00:00:52.718 --> 00:00:54.920
There's no worries.

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:56.322
I went to Missouri.

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:58.157
-Whoo!
-Learned a lot.

00:00:58.157 --> 00:01:00.326
It should be, "If you can
make it in Missouri."

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:01.961
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:04.397
Fam, you've earned that.

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:06.065
That's hard work.

00:01:06.065 --> 00:01:08.267
How you gon' sell your mix tape
if nobody outside?

00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:11.070
There is no one outside.

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:12.305
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:15.008
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:19.212 --> 00:01:21.013
Missouri was a learning
experience, man.

00:01:21.013 --> 00:01:23.449
That was the first time
I seen a vulture in person.

00:01:23.449 --> 00:01:24.950
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:26.051
That's a pivotal moment.

00:01:26.051 --> 00:01:28.421
Vultures are a TV bird,
you know?

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:30.756
You supposed to only see that
on television.

00:01:30.756 --> 00:01:35.628
I casually saw one in my regular
life, just at a gas station.

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:38.397
I didn't know what to do.
I just waved at it.

00:01:38.397 --> 00:01:39.998
I'm a New Yorker.
I don't do it right.

00:01:39.998 --> 00:01:42.068
New Yorkers don't wave.
I'm just like under-handed.

00:01:42.068 --> 00:01:43.636
"Hey, buddy.

00:01:43.636 --> 00:01:46.105
I don't want any trouble, man."

00:01:46.105 --> 00:01:47.473
But, honest,

00:01:47.473 --> 00:01:50.510
vultures are negative.
They're negative birds.

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:52.145
The entire time
they looking at you,

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:55.014
they just like,
"Yo, I hope you die, bro.

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:57.650
Ooh, I can't wait."

00:01:57.650 --> 00:01:59.952
Worst thing New York got
is some pigeons.

00:01:59.952 --> 00:02:02.254
You can find videos of them
stepping aside politely

00:02:02.254 --> 00:02:03.489
to let you on the train.

00:02:03.489 --> 00:02:04.623
They got
their little wings back.

00:02:04.623 --> 00:02:06.626
"What's up, brother?
I understand.

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:09.362
It's alright."

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:11.464
It's easy. It's not that bad.

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:13.365
Took a trip upstate New York.

00:02:13.365 --> 00:02:15.167
-Whoo!
-Six hours.

00:02:15.167 --> 00:02:17.536
Six hours on this train.

00:02:17.536 --> 00:02:19.906
I learned, though, if you travel
a minimum of two hours

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:23.176
in any direction out the city,
it turns into Alabama quickly.

00:02:23.176 --> 00:02:24.810
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:26.646
So fast.

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:28.748
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.083 --> 00:02:32.385
I'm used to taking the trains.

00:02:32.385 --> 00:02:34.487
I grew up in New York,
always took a train.

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:35.921
You know, you take the trains
out here,

00:02:35.921 --> 00:02:37.957
you probably got robbed
for your phone or something,

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:39.459
but you made your destination.

00:02:39.459 --> 00:02:40.693
You can just walk.

00:02:40.693 --> 00:02:42.128
Took the train upstate New York,

00:02:42.128 --> 00:02:44.564
and they just let me out
at a forest.

00:02:44.564 --> 00:02:45.664
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:45.664 --> 00:02:47.599
Just a forest, bro.

00:02:47.599 --> 00:02:49.602
I don't have forest experience.

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:52.738
I don't know about foliage.
Nothing.

00:02:52.738 --> 00:02:55.475
All my skills are made
for New York City.

00:02:55.475 --> 00:02:58.444
I can hop a turnstile.
I can't find North.

00:02:58.444 --> 00:03:00.680
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:03.316
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:09.522
I know who I am, you understand?

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:11.990
You know what I'm saying? I can
spot bad deli meat a mile away,

00:03:11.990 --> 00:03:13.859
wouldn't even ruin me.

00:03:13.859 --> 00:03:16.329
You pull a knife on me,
I'll fight you.

00:03:16.329 --> 00:03:19.565
If you threw a raccoon my way,
though, alright.

00:03:19.565 --> 00:03:21.367
Okay. Fighting dirty now.

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:23.636
Use a knife like a gentleman.
Come on, now.

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:24.904
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.904 --> 00:03:26.505
It was terrible
walking through that forest.

00:03:26.505 --> 00:03:29.008
I didn't know anything about it.
No forest experience.

00:03:29.008 --> 00:03:31.044
I don't know
what trees not to touch.

00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:32.478
I don't know what's poison.

00:03:32.478 --> 00:03:36.081
My only reference of poison
is Bell Biv DeVoe.

00:03:36.081 --> 00:03:39.485
I'm gonna die out there.

00:03:39.485 --> 00:03:41.154
I know better.

00:03:41.154 --> 00:03:42.888
I was scared. I was walking
through that forest.

00:03:42.888 --> 00:03:44.089
I checked my phone.

00:03:44.089 --> 00:03:47.727
My phone was on 23%.

00:03:47.727 --> 00:03:50.029
My heart sank.

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:52.865
'Cause I knew right then
and there, if my phone die,

00:03:52.865 --> 00:03:54.534
this is where I live now.

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:57.870
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:01.607
I do not possess the skills to
find my way home using nature.

00:04:01.607 --> 00:04:04.076
That is not gon' happen.

00:04:04.076 --> 00:04:05.344
Not gon' be able
to look at the forest

00:04:05.344 --> 00:04:08.047
and know where trees grow moss.
Nothing. Done.

00:04:08.047 --> 00:04:10.283
I called my boy up.
I needed some help.

00:04:10.283 --> 00:04:12.285
Worst advice ever.

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:14.353
I'm like, "Yo, bro, I'm scared.
I don't know what to do."

00:04:14.353 --> 00:04:16.555
He's like, "You scared, bro?"

00:04:16.555 --> 00:04:19.558
You from New York.
How you scared of a forest?"

00:04:19.558 --> 00:04:21.494
"You scared of a --"
Yes.

00:04:21.494 --> 00:04:23.028
What you expect me to do?
Run into a bear

00:04:23.028 --> 00:04:25.564
and be like, "Wait, bro!
I'm from Brooklyn, son!

00:04:25.564 --> 00:04:28.233
None of that roar!
None of that, not with me!

00:04:28.233 --> 00:04:30.069
Nah."
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:32.171
Thank you guys. Thank you.

00:04:32.171 --> 00:04:34.306
♪♪

00:04:34.306 --> 00:04:38.210
-Thanks, man! You were great!
You look great.

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:41.381
Andre D Thompson!

00:04:41.381 --> 00:04:43.416
"Between Spots"
is available on Spotify.

